\details{
Provides methods for retrieving margin-specific market data from Binance,
including cross/isolated margin pairs, price indices, interest rate history,
and margin data summaries.

Inherits from \link{BinanceBase}. All methods support both synchronous and
asynchronous execution depending on the \code{async} parameter at construction.
\subsection{Purpose and Scope}{
\itemize{
\item \strong{Margin Pairs}: Retrieve available cross and isolated margin trading pairs.
\item \strong{Price Index}: Access margin price index for a symbol.
\item \strong{Interest Rates}: Get historical interest rate data for margin borrowing.
\item \strong{Margin Data}: Retrieve cross and isolated margin data including borrowing limits and interest rates.
}
}

\subsection{Usage}{

Most methods require authentication (valid API key and secret).
\code{get_price_index} is a public endpoint requiring no authentication.
}

\subsection{Official Documentation}{

\href{https://binance-docs.github.io/apidocs/spot/en/#margin-account-trade}{Binance Margin Account/Trade}
}

